class Solution {
    public int maxOperations(int[] nums, int k) {
        // Sort the array first
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        
        int left=0; // pointer at the start
        int right=nums.length-1; // pointer at the end
        int ct=0; // number of valid pairs
        
        while(left<right){
            int sum = nums[left] + nums[right];
            if(sum==k){
                // Found a valid pair
                ct++;
                left++;
                right--;
            }
            else if(sum<k){
                // Need a larger sum → move left pointer right
                left++;
            }else{
                // Need a smaller sum → move right pointer left
                right--;
            }
        }
        return ct;
    }
}


Time Complexity: O(n log n) (due to sorting).
Space Complexity: O(1) (in‑place, just pointers).
